---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../data/site';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Article',
    headline: 'Fill long forms with HailBrowser Fast mode',
    description:
      'Give HailBrowser the goal and the values. The decision model picks one operation and one element per step, with no selectors and no text model.',
    dateModified: '2026-10-30',
    author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'HailBrowser contributors' },
    mainEntityOfPage: `${SITE.url}/use-cases/form-flows`,
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: `${SITE.url}/` },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Use cases', item: `${SITE.url}/use-cases` },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'Form flows', item: `${SITE.url}/use-cases/form-flows` },
    ],
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Fill long forms without a text model"
  description="HailBrowser Fast mode drives a form with one decision request per step: operation plus element index, never a selector or coordinate. Pass the values once."
  type="article"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <div class="frame">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/use-cases">Use cases</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">Form flows</span>
    </nav>

    <header class="page-hero">
      <div class="page-hero__meta">
        <span class="pill pill--ink">Use case 04</span>
        <span class="pill">Fast mode · one request per step</span>
      </div>
      <h1>Fill the form once.<br />Not field by field.</h1>
      <p>
        A booking form, a claims page, a supplier portal. Give HailBrowser the values and let a decision
        model pick the field and the text, without a frontier model on every keystroke.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="split split--wide-right">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>The goal and the values</h2>
        <CodeBlock
          code={`{
  "goal": "Search one-way flights for 1 adult",
  "mode": "ultrafast",
  "values": {
    "From": "Zurich",
    "To": "London",
    "Date": "2026-09-20"
  }
}`}
          file="run_task · arguments"
          lang="json"
          label="The whole form, in four lines"
        />
        <p>
          This is also the shape a coding agent passes through MCP. In the side panel, say the same thing
          in a sentence and switch the composer to <strong>Fast</strong>.
        </p>

        <h2>What happens</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>The page becomes an indexed table of elements: role, name, value, placeholder.</li>
          <li>The decision model returns one operation and one element index, for example <code>TYPE_TEXT [4]</code>.</li>
          <li>The executor checks that the page and the target are unchanged, types the value with real key events, and observes what happened.</li>
          <li>A field that rejected the value is reported. A moved button costs another decision, not a misclick.</li>
          <li>When the goal is reached, a <code>DONE</code> claim gets a second yes/no check before the run reports success.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2>Field names do the boring work</h2>
        <p>
          A field named like a value key is filled without a model call. “Where to?” matches
          <code>To</code>, “Departure date” matches <code>Date</code>. The text is taken from your goal and
          values only, never from page text, so a page cannot inject a value into a field.
        </p>

        <h2>What to check</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>The values, before you submit. Watch the fields fill on the first run.</li>
          <li>That the date format matched what the site wanted. A rejected value is reported, but a plausible wrong one is not.</li>
          <li>The confirmation page, not the model's summary of it.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>What can go wrong</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>A custom date picker.</strong> Some pickers are canvas or shadow DOM; Fast may miss them. Fill that field by hand and re-run from there.</li>
          <li><strong>A cross-origin iframe.</strong> Payment and login widgets often sit in one. The field is not in the indexed table.</li>
          <li><strong>A file upload.</strong> There is no upload tool, so a form that needs a document stops at that step.</li>
          <li><strong>A CAPTCHA.</strong> Fast cannot solve it. Stop, solve it yourself, and resume.</li>
          <li><strong>A validation you cannot see.</strong> The run reports a rejected value when the page changes; silent validation needs a human look.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <aside class="stack" style="align-content:start">
        <div class="callout">
          <p class="label">Why it is cheap</p>
          <p>
            One decision request per step, and no text model when values come from the goal. That is the
            difference between Fast and Chat.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="callout">
          <p class="label">Tools in this guide</p>
          <ul class="tool-links">
            <li><a href="/docs/mcp#tool-run_task">run_task</a></li>
            <li><a href="/docs/mcp#tool-read_page">read_page</a></li>
            <li><a href="/docs/mcp#tool-type">type</a></li>
            <li><a href="/docs/mcp#tool-select_option">select_option</a></li>
            <li><a href="/docs/mcp#tool-press_key">press_key</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="callout">
          <p class="label">Five backends</p>
          <p>
            Decision API, OpenRouter, Inception, a letter-choice classifier, or any LLM.
            <a class="link" href="/docs/modes#fast">How to choose <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>

    <section class="section section--tight">
      <nav class="more-links" aria-label="Related">
        <a href="/use-cases/coding-agents">
          <span class="label">Next</span>
          <b>Coding agents</b>
          <em>Let your agent hand over the form.</em>
        </a>
        <a href="/docs/modes#fast">
          <span class="label">Behaviour</span>
          <b>Fast mode</b>
          <em>One decision per step, explained.</em>
        </a>
        <a href="/docs/mcp#tool-run_task">
          <span class="label">Reference</span>
          <b>run_task</b>
          <em>Goal, mode, url, values, tabId.</em>
        </a>
        <a href="/docs/limits">
          <span class="label">Honest</span>
          <b>Limits</b>
          <em>iframes, canvas and uploads.</em>
        </a>
      </nav>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
